WEBVTT

unit-0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
The next match features Tenmu Moka and Tachikawa. Come on, Moka, do your best! Earlier, Tachikawa also showed his professionalism and pride.

unit-0002
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
He really showed his professionalism. I was looking at something with Tachikawa's image on it, and it was quite something. Tachikawa, you're amazing.

unit-0003
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
He was talking about something from way back – like, five years ago. He mentioned a livestream raid, and he was saying something about finding someone to do it with. Apparently, there's a VTuber with a bird perched on their shoulder.

unit-0004
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:43.200
<v SPEAKER_00>Apparently, they started playing with that kind of vibe – like, "let's do this." Then, they started suggesting something like, "Want to play Portal together?"

unit-0005
00:00:47.136 --> 00:01:03.040
<v SPEAKER_00>Could you send me something quickly?

unit-0006
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:11.380
<v SPEAKER_00>"Hey, it's like, 'aren't you two really close?' It's almost like you're a couple." From my perspective, it's Go and Shiro.

unit-0007
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:17.460
<v SPEAKER_02>The combination of I and Mai is genuinely amusing. And I suppose Tatsuya is doing modern dance, which is great. It's wonderful to have encounters like that – modern dance.

unit-0008
00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.860
<v SPEAKER_02>It's amusing to see them getting along so well. It's quite something to witness their interactions here. It really highlights their unique approach – a powerful, one-move technique.

unit-0009
00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.060
<v SPEAKER_00>That's it.

unit-0010
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:34.740
<v SPEAKER_01>Alright, let's get ready. We have Aime, and then Tachikawa. Let's take a look at this highly anticipated match. Let's see, Tachikawa is...

unit-0011
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.100
<v SPEAKER_01>Let's focus on the department head's match.

unit-0012
00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.380
<v SPEAKER_01>Alright, Aime. No need to rush. Let's disrupt their momentum with a strong attack. Keep it up!

unit-0013
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.780
<v SPEAKER_01>Tatara will move forward.

unit-0014
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.340
That's good. That's fine.

unit-0015
00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:58.740
<v SPEAKER_01>He came from the lead to recover his pace. Both drivers need to be careful about when to pit.

unit-0016
00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.120
<v SPEAKER_01>Stay calm, and both drivers will need to increase their distance. Well done.

unit-0017
00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.800
<v SPEAKER_01>Coming from behind after a long battle, he's closing in. There's still some room to maneuver.

unit-0018
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:17.200
<v SPEAKER_02>If you synchronize your punches, that's a viable counter. It's a way to avoid it by using a vertical jump, but it's also effective to use that space while jumping forward.

unit-0019
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.160
<v SPEAKER_01>This is difficult to counter. Both sides are being very cautious.

unit-0020
00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:34.045
<v SPEAKER_01>Amari (likely a name) has a lot of drive, but it feels a little slow. I wonder what amazing things she's going to do. She's using her drive against the opponent.

unit-0021
00:02:34.194 --> 00:02:43.520
<v SPEAKER_00>That department head's battle is dangerous. It seems like they're carefully managing this area. Be cautious when approaching; don't overdo it until then.

unit-0022
00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:50.640
<v SPEAKER_00>"Wow, we're in a situation where time is really limited. That place, huh? We still have time. Twenty seconds left. Let's go like this."

